   "summary": "The incident occurred on Saturday, November 14, 2026, at Ruga Village in Gwana District, where the Chinese national was reportedly engaged in core drilling activities as part of a mining site survey. The Bauchi State Police Command confirmed the attack, saying the company vehicle conveying the expatriate was ambushed by suspected bandits while security personnel were escorting him.",
   "summary_zh": "事件发生于2026年11月14日星期六，地点是Gwana区的Ruga村。据报道，这名中国籍男子当时正从事岩芯钻探活动，作为矿区勘察的一部分。包奇州警察司令部证实了此次袭击，称安保人员护送该外籍人士时，载有他的公司车辆遭疑似土匪伏击。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The incident occurred on Saturday, November 14, 2026, at Ruga Village in Gwana District, where the Chinese national was reportedly engaged in core drilling activities as part of a mining site survey. The Bauchi State Police Command confirmed the attack, saying the company vehicle conveying the expatriate was ambushed by suspected bandits while security personnel were escorting him. The Police Public Relations Officer (PPRO), SP Nafiu Habib, while confirming the incident in a telephone conversation with LEADERSHIP on Monday, explaining that the attack resulted in an exchange of gunfire between the security operatives and the assailants. “Yes, it is true that the incident occurred on Saturday. The team was ambushed, and following an exchange of gunfire between the security personnel escorting the miner and the assailants, the miner and one police officer lost their lives,” he said. Habib disclosed that the incident took place in Gwana District while the mining team was in the area to conduct a survey at a mining site. The police inspector, identified as Yau Abba, was attached to the Mobile Police Force (MOPOL) 34 and deployed to provide security for the Chinese national. According to the report, efforts were ongoing to track down and arrest those responsible for the attack, while security agencies were working to establish the circumstances surrounding the incident. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
