   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription India’s central bank on Friday (November 13, 2026) filed a petition in the country’s apex court seeking a review of its judgment that set aside the write-off of 84.15 billion rupees ($893.8 million) of Yes Bank’s additional tier-1 bonds, the court’s website showed on Monday (November 16, 2026). Last month, the Supreme Court had upheld a Bombay High Court ruling which had set aside the write-off of Yes Bank’s AT-1 bonds and said the write-off was impermissible.",
   "summary_zh": "Subscription India中央银行于星期五（2026年11月13日）向该国最高法院提交请愿书，请求复核法院撤销Yes Bank价值841.5亿卢比（8.938亿美元）的额外一级资本债券注销交易的判决。法院网站于星期一（2026年11月16日）显示了这项请愿。上个月，最高法院维持了孟买高等法院的一项裁决；该裁决撤销了Yes Bank额外一级资本债券的注销，并认定注销该债券不当。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription India’s central bank on Friday (November 13, 2026) filed a petition in the country’s apex court seeking a review of its judgment that set aside the write-off of 84.15 billion rupees ($893.8 million) of Yes Bank’s additional tier-1 bonds, the court’s website showed on Monday (November 16, 2026). An email query sent to the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) was not answered. Last month, the Supreme Court had upheld a Bombay High Court ruling which had set aside the write-off of Yes Bank’s AT-1 bonds and said the write-off was impermissible. Yes Bank, in which Japan’s Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corporation now holds a 24% stake, was declared insolvent six years ago; as part of a restructuring scheme, new investors were brought in and its AT-1 bonds were written off. On Friday (November 13, 2026), Yes Bank informed exchanges that it had filed a review petition without disclosing the grounds for seeking relief. Earlier this month, Axis Trustee Services, acting on behalf of the bondholders, filed a contempt petition in the Supreme Court alleging Yes Bank’s failure to provide a “concrete roadmap” for restoring the bonds and implementing the court’s judgment. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
