   "title": "Hungarian authorities uncover $20m during probe of Orbán-era minister",
   "url": "https://www.myjoyonline.com/hungarian-authorities-uncover-20m-during-probe-of-orban-era-minister/",
   "domain": "myjoyonline.com",
   "source": "MyJoyOnline（加纳）",
   "published": "Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:36:03 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794674163.0,
   "ageDays": 2.07,
   "summary": "Nearly $20m (£14.8m) in cash has been found hidden in farm buildings and buried in forests as part of an investigation into a former minister of Viktor Orbán, authorities have said. Miklós Seszták, who served as minister of national development for four of the ex-prime minister's 16-year rule, is accused of accepting bribes as part of a scheme involving the state transport company. On Monday, Hungarian authorities also detained Orbán's brother and three others as part of a people-smuggling case.",
   "summary_zh": "当局表示，在调查维克托·欧尔班政府时期一名前部长一案时，人们在农场建筑内和森林中发现了近2000万美元（1480万英镑）现金。Miklós Seszták 在这位前总理16年执政期间有4年担任国家发展部长，他被指控在涉及国家运输公司的计划中收受贿赂。周一，匈牙利当局还在一桩偷渡人口案件中拘留了欧尔班的弟弟及另外3人。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Nearly $20m (£14.8m) in cash has been found hidden in farm buildings and buried in forests as part of an investigation into a former minister of Viktor Orbán, authorities have said. Miklós Seszták, who served as minister of national development for four of the ex-prime minister's 16-year rule, is accused of accepting bribes as part of a scheme involving the state transport company. He has denied any wrongdoing. Hungary's new Prime Minister Péter Magyar unseated Orbán in a landslide election in April on the promise of launching a sweeping anti-corruption drive. On Friday, following the two-day search for the cash - found in secluded locations across the country - Magyar described it as the end of the \"mafia\". Investigators found wads of banknotes in safes, buried in woodlands and hidden in agricultural and residential buildings and warehouses, as part of the probe into Seszták, the National Asset Recovery and Protection Office (NVVH) said in a statement. The cash amounted to \"5,071,632,000 forints, €2,658,350 and $1,257,100\", it added, bringing the combined value to $19.5m. It has been deposited into the Hungarian State Treasury, the body said. The NVVH was established to investigate allegations of corruption during the Orbán rule, which Magyar has dubbed \"Operation Purgatory\". Magyar promised Hungarians \"regime change\" during the election earlier this year and has set about undoing many Orbán-era policies since entering office. Allegations of corruption and cronyism have long dogged Orbán, who during the course of his tenure turned Hungary into what the EU characterised as an \"electoral autocracy\". His government faced accusations of offering lucrative government projects to allies. Orbán has strongly denied the claims. Two of his former ministers, including Seszták, and the former central bank chief Gyorgy Matolcsyhave been under arrest since September over accusations of graft in separate investigations. They all deny wrongdoing. On Monday, Hungarian authorities also detained Orbán's brother and three others as part of a people-smuggling case. The former prime minister dismissed it as political revenge, saying: \"In this dirty game, the aim is the elimination of the political opponent and the establishment of a one-party system",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "eu"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_myjoyonline",
   "title_zh": "调查欧尔班时代部长期间，匈牙利当局发现2000万美元",
   "body_zh": "当局表示，在调查前总理维克托·欧尔班（Viktor Orbán）的一名前部长时，执法人员在全国多地的农舍建筑内发现近2000万美元（1480万英镑）现金，并在森林中挖出藏匿的钱款。曾在欧尔班16年执政期间担任4年国家发展部长的米克洛什·谢斯塔克（Miklós Seszták）被指控在一项涉及国家运输公司的计划中收受贿赂。他否认有任何不当行为。匈牙利新任总理彼得·马扎尔（Péter Magyar）在4月举行的选举中以压倒性优势击败欧尔班，并承诺开展大规模反腐败行动。周五，在持续两天的现金搜寻行动结束后，马扎尔称此举意味着“黑手党”的末日。搜寻人员在全国偏远地区发现了成捆钞票，这些钱藏在保险箱中、埋于林地，并藏在农业建筑、住宅建筑和仓库内。国家资产追回与保护办公室（NVVH）在一份声明中表示，这是对谢斯塔克展开调查的一部分。声明称，这些现金包括“5,071,632,632,000福林、€2,658,350和$1,257,100”，总价值达到1950万美元。该机构表示，这笔钱已存入匈牙利国库。NVVH的成立是为了调查欧尔班执政期间的腐败指控，马扎尔将这场行动称为“炼狱行动”。马扎尔在今年早些时候的选举中向匈牙利人承诺实现“政权更替”，上任后已开始撤销欧尔班时期的许多政策。长期以来，腐败和任人唯亲的指控一直困扰着欧尔班；在其任内，匈牙利被欧盟定性为“选举威权国家”。欧尔班政府曾被指控将利润丰厚的政府项目交给盟友。欧尔班强烈否认这些指控。他的两名前部长，包括谢斯塔克，以及前中央银行行长久尔吉·马托尔奇（Gyorgy Matolcsy），自9月以来因分别涉及贪腐的调查而遭到逮捕。他们均否认存在不当行为。周一，匈牙利当局还在一宗偷渡人口案件中拘捕了欧尔班的弟弟及另外3人。这位前总理斥此事为政治报复，并称：“在这场肮脏的博弈中，目的是消灭政治对手、建立一党制",
   "snippet_zh": ""
