   "title": "Wike’s 700-Man Campaign Council Targets 4m Votes for Tinubu, Says APC Chieftain",
   "url": "https://www.thisdaylive.com/2026/11/14/wikes-700-man-campaign-council-targets-4m-votes-for-tinubu-says-apc-chieftain/",
   "domain": "thisdaylive.com",
   "source": "ThisDay（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:37:57 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794667077.0,
   "ageDays": 2.15,
   "summary": "An All Progressives Congress (APC) chieftain in Rivers State, Princewill Dike, has said the 700-member APC Presidential/Rivers Rainbow Coalition Candidates Campaign Council constituted by the Minister of the Federal Capital Territory (FCT), Nyesom Wike, is targeting at least four million votes for President Bola Tinubu in the 2027 general election.",
   "summary_zh": "Rivers State 的全进步大会党（APC）党魁普林威尔·戴克表示，由联邦首都地区（FCT）部长涅松·威克组建的700人APC总统选举暨河流州彩虹联盟候选人竞选委员会，正以在2027年大选中为博拉·提努布总统争取至少400万张选票为目标。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "An All Progressives Congress (APC) chieftain in Rivers State, Princewill Dike, has said the 700-member APC Presidential/Rivers Rainbow Coalition Candidates Campaign Council constituted by the Minister of the Federal Capital Territory (FCT), Nyesom Wike, is targeting at least four million votes for President Bola Tinubu in the 2027 general election. Dike, who spoke in Port Harcourt on Friday, described the council as a strategic grassroots mobilisation structure designed to take the campaign beyond political rallies and directly engage voters across Rivers State. He said the council’s numerical strength should not be mistaken for a ceremonial political arrangement, stressing that its effectiveness would depend on members’ ability to translate their appointments into tangible grassroots mobilisation. According to him, Wike’s political approach is rooted in strategic organisation, coalition-building and sustained engagement with the electorate. “For Wike, politics is more than an occasional engagement; it is a calculated enterprise that demands constant attention, strategic thinking, organisation and an understanding of the dynamics of power,” Dike said. He explained that members of the council would be expected to embark on door-to-door campaigns and engage different segments of the electorate, including traders, transport operators and residents in their communities. “The objective is to ensure that political communication extends to every community where eligible voters reside,” he added. Dike said the initiative was intended to establish a formidable campaign network capable of reaching voters in every part of the state and persuading them to support Tinubu and candidates of the Rivers Rainbow Coalition. He noted that direct voter engagement, persuasion and personal political relationships would be critical to translating political structures into electoral victories. The APC chieftain also disclosed that Wike planned to establish campaign councils at the local government and ward levels to broaden participation and strengthen coordination from the state to the grassroots. Dike expressed optimism that effective implementation of the mobilisation strategy could deliver an unprecedented electoral performance for Tinubu and the Rivers Rainbow Coalition in 2027. However, he cautioned that the success of the 700-member council would depend not on its size but on the commitment and performance of its members. “A 700-member council can only justify its size when members demonstrate commitment, discipline, coordination and a willingness to engage voters at the community level,” he said. Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "cor"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_thisday",
   "title_zh": "全进步人民党首领称，怀克的700人竞选委员会计划为蒂努布争取400万张选票",
   "body_zh": "尼日利亚（尼日利亚，首都阿布贾）河州全进步大会党（APC）领导人Princewill Dike表示，由联邦首都领地（FCT）部长Nyesom Wike组建、拥有700名成员的“APC总统/河州彩虹联盟候选人竞选委员会”，计划在2027年大选中为总统Bola Tinobu争取至少400万张选票。Dike周五在哈科特Port Harcourt发表讲话，将该委员会称为一项战略性基层动员架构，旨在把竞选活动拓展到政治集会之外，直接接触河州各地选民。他说，不应将委员会庞大的人数误认为一种仪式性的政治安排，并强调其成效取决于成员能否将任命转化为切实的基层动员行动。据他介绍，Wike的政治路线以战略组织、建立联盟以及持续与选民互动为基础。Dike说：“对Wike而言，政治不仅仅是偶尔参与的活动，而是一项经过谋划的事业，需要持续关注、战略思维、组织能力以及对权力动态的理解。”他解释说，委员会成员应当开展挨家挨户的外展活动，并接触选民中的不同群体，包括商人、交通运营商和各自社区的居民。他补充道：“目标是确保政治沟通延伸到每一个有合格选民居住的社区。”Dike表示，这项倡议旨在建立一个强大的竞选网络，能够接触该州各地的选民，说服他们支持Tinobu以及河州彩虹联盟的候选人。他指出，直接接触选民、争取其支持以及建立个人政治关系，是把政治架构转化为选举胜利的关键。这名APC领导人还透露，Wike计划在地方政府一级和选区一级设立竞选委员会，以扩大参与范围，并加强从州级到基层的协调工作。Dike乐观认为，如果有效落实这项动员战略，Tinobu和河州彩虹联盟有望在2027年取得前所未有的选举佳绩。不过他警告说，700人委员会能否成功并不取决于其规模，而取决于成员的投入程度和工作表现。他说：“只有当成员展现出投入精神、纪律、协作以及在社区层面接触选民的意愿时，700人委员会才能证明其规模的价值。”THISDAY创刊于1995年1月22日，由THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD.出版，地址为尼日利亚（尼日利亚，首都阿布贾）拉各斯阿帕帕Creek Road 35号，并在尼日利亚36个州、联邦首都领地以及世界各地设有办公室。作为尼日利亚最权威的新闻媒体，THISDAY通过所有平台面向政治、商业、专业和外交精英以及更广泛的中产阶级受众，报道时事、商业、市场、艺术、体育和社区议题，服务于社会与人交汇的领域，并充当新思想、文化和技术的交汇点，陪伴志向者与千禧一代共同成长。该报秉持公共信托精神，致力于追求真相与理性，报道范围涵盖突发新闻、政治、商业、市场、艺术、体育和社区等议题。您可以发送邮件至：hello@thisdaylive.com，或访问我们的联系我们页面",
